```

Thus a new-coordinate monomial `x^e y^k` has probe weight `e-k`.  P.209 places
this probe in the selected minor disc `D_2^*`, so its center lies strictly over

 succeeded in 0ms:
```text
0<=k<=D,             4k-D <= e <= 2D+k,
```

but membership in this envelope is not sufficient, because inverse-image
coefficients are correlated.

Combining the top and radius-two weights gives the following useful maximal
