xmodel/block-descent-a1-rank4-reducible-component-tree-ledger-hostile-review-sol56-20260831.md:114:Using the promoted specialization rule more precisely makes the omission sharper. A point on the closure of a `T31` component is still in `T31` when its fibre remains `(3,1)`; a mixed component intersection is not automatically a puncture. Specialization from generic `(3,1)` to `(2,1,1)` is forbidden, and `S22` is forbidden on that component, so only `S4` points puncture it. Thus the safe exact form is
