xmodel/as109-cubic-review-grok-20260824.md:377:*Correction `y`-degree implies coordinate `y`-degree.* View `P,Q` in `Q_{109}[x,y]`. The summand `x-x^{109}` is independent of `y`, and `109 \neq 0` in `Q_{109}`, so `deg_y(P)=deg_y(A)` if `deg_y(A)>=1`, and `deg_y(P)=0` otherwise. Likewise `deg_y(Q)=max(1, deg_y(B))` except possibly if the linear term of `109 B` cancelled the seed `y`. That cancellation would *drop* degree, so `deg_y(Q)<=3` still. (For completeness: it cannot occur for integral `B`, because the coefficient of `y` in `Q` is `1+109 b_1(x)` with `b_1 in Z_{109}[x]`, and `-1/109` is not in `Z_{109}`.) Thus `deg_y(P), deg_y(Q)<=3`. The identity `det J(F)=1` survives `Z_{109} -> Q_{109}`. Claim 5 over `K=Q_{109}` makes `F` a polynomial automorphism of `A^2_{Q_{109}}`, hence injective on `Q_{109}^2`.
