xmodel/max12-812-order2-square-a-prolongation-hostile-review-grok-20260826.md:341:Radicalization discards the scheme thickness recorded by the 448-element standard basis. It does not invalidate the pointwise exclusion: `a0,a1` in the radical means every geometric point of the localized source scheme has `A0=0`. Nilpotents are thickness over that reduced support, not an extra reduced component with `A0≠0`. Design §3 required that grade fourteen not be replaced by its radical before adjoining grade fifteen; the producer adjoins both complete grades first, then saturates, then radicalizes. Root-allocation faces of `(2.2)` are retained through that adjunction and are killed by grade fifteen, in agreement with §5.
