xmodel/max12-812-order2-square-d1-c2-c8-first-connection-hostile-review-grok-20260826.md:174:Jet ceilings are mechanical from the grade-25 family `k6*C`. The substitutions retained through grade 26 are `k6=k60+σ k60_1`, `C=σ^8(C_0+σ C_1)`, and `p(σ)=p+2σ ell1`. Next-`A`, next-`R`, `k60_2`, and `ell2` first affect polar source at grade 27. `AC`, `C^2`, and `RC` themselves first appear at grade 26, so their own next jets are at 27 or later. The compiled numerator sentinels `diff(N2, k60_1)`, `diff(N2, cc1)`, `diff(N2, cc0)`, `diff(N2, ell1)` are therefore the complete in-window jet list; all four are nonzero.
