xmodel/max12-812-order2-p0-total-rees-t-rs0-discovery-implementation-review-grok-20260826.md:209:| Dependency manifest | `subst(TPhi, name, 0) != TPhi` for every candidate | **Holds.** Support of the unextracted prefix is the support of `{G_0,…,G_12}` because the `sigma`-grades cannot cancel. `discovered_manifest` is that support, in order, and is enough to freeze a minimal V1 list. Two-prime vanishing of a coefficient is a characteristic issue, not a `subst` bug; see §8. Ring variables are distinct atoms (`k` vs `k1` vs `k2c` vs `k10_3`; `k2` vs `k2c`); `subst` is not a string prefix. If it were, `subst(k2,0)` would hit `k2c` and the inactive bit would fail closed |
xmodel/max12-812-order2-p0-total-rees-t-rs0-discovery-implementation-review-grok-20260826.md:247:| Minimal support among the 76 candidates | support modulo `{32003,65521}`; a coefficient in `(32003*65521)` can vanish at both primes | the actual support | the prefix equations `E_12` |
