xmodel/max12-812-order2-square-d1-a9-d23-j38-r3-tail-hostile-review-grok-20260826.md:283:Substituting `eta=sigma^s` with `s>=0` raises `ord(R)` from 9 to `9+s`. Families with `R`-exponent zero (`k6 C`, unloaded `A C`, `k10 A^2`, unloaded `C^2`, `k10 A C`, `k2 A`, `k10 C^2`, `k2 C`) are unchanged. Families with positive `R`-exponent are delayed by `s` times that exponent. The contributing set at `ord(R)>=9` is therefore a subset of the `ord(R)=9` window after a nonnegative grade shift. Pole ceiling three and target placement are preserved; the first pole-four wall only moves later. Targets do not depend on `R`.
