xmodel/max12-812-order2-square-d1-unitload-contact-ladder-composition-hostile-review-grok-20260826.md:193:**No early `k6` at `a<=5`.** `k6 C/L` has order `18+a`. The two-grade window ends at `12+2a`. For `a=5` this is 23 against 22; for `a<=4` the gap is larger. `k6 R^2/L` is at `>=16+2a`, gap 4. `k2`, `mu2`, `mu4`, `mu6`, `J` all lie after `g+1` in this band. The CONFIRMED review charges 336 `diff` tests on the complete seven-row source, not an order table alone. There is no silent `k6` section.
