codex
Moh p.209’s image confirms the radius-two branch data and the transform text; that is a control source, not the δ=5/2 case itself. Now I’m checking Xu p.13 visually and then I’ll build the symbolic reduced-ODE verifier.
codex
I’m moving from the source read into the algebra. The first durable check will be Xu’s reduced ODE and the immediate half-order deformation `D_s(Q,h) = -2s^2 h^4`, where `s^2=t`; this is a local necessary/superset test unless the full approximate-root bridge is also imposed.
